22
00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:35.720
Why He Really Did It. Vietnam War was bleeding money. France wanted their gold back (party poopers).

23
00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:41.180
Couldn't raise taxes (people riot). Solution: Print money forever!

24
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:47.430
What Actually Happened. Gold standard: Dead. Dollar backing: "Trust us bro".

25
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:55.180
Inflation: To the moon. Your savings: Slowly murdered. The Theft That Followed.

26
00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:01.620
Since nineteen seventy-two: Productivity up: two hundred forty-six percent.

27
00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.500
Wages up: one hundred fifteen percent. The difference: They stole it.

28
00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.510
Where'd the money go? Three guesses: Wall Street (correct!).

29
00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:18.760
War contractors (also correct!). You (BZZT! Wrong! Thanks for playing!).

30
00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:28.480
The Cantillon Effect: Why You're Poor and Raytheon Isn't. The Cantillon Effect, understood since the seventeen hundreds:

31
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:34.180
whoever gets newly printed money first gets rich. Whoever gets it last gets robbed.

32
00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:41.980
The Fed prints money. Banks and defense contractors get it first and buy things at today's prices.

33
00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.500
By the time it trickles down to your grocery store, prices have already risen.

34
00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.520
You don't notice you've been robbed because nobody broke into your house.

35
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.480
They just made everything in it worth less. Then you blame immigrants.

36
00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.980
Which is exactly what they want you to do. (The immigrants also got robbed, by the way.

37
00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:07.260
You have so much in common.). Why "Just Fund Medical Research More" Is a Lie.

38
00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:12.440
"Why not just ask for donations? Why not just increase the N.I.H.

39
00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:18.720
budget? Why tie it to military spending?". Because money is not real.

40
00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:26.670
It's a shared hallucination. Eight billion people pretending that the same piece of paper is worth something.

41
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:34.860
Resources are real. Brains are real. Time is real. Money is a story you tell each other.

42
00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:43.200
The Fixed Pie of Human Genius. Earth has eight billion brains (fixed quantity).

43
00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:49.000
There are twenty-four hours per day per brain (physics won't negotiate).

44
00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:59.800
There are limited raw materials (can't print titanium). There is finite factory capacity (can't build infinite labs).

45
00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:06.460
When a brilliant engineer designs missiles, that engineer is NOT designing medical devices.

46
00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:11.280
When a factory builds tanks, it is NOT building M.R.I. machines.

47
00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:19.160
When a PhD researches better ways to kill people, they are NOT researching better ways to keep people alive.

48
00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:27.980
Every genius has exactly one brain. You are renting forty million of them to build things that explode.

49
00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:35.500
This is, by a comfortable margin, the stupidest resource allocation decision in the observable universe.

50
00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:43.740
The Resource Reality. The top ten percent of human talent is approximately eight hundred million people.

51
00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:52.020
There are currently forty million people building weapons. There is approximately one million people currently curing disease.

52
00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:59.200
The ratio is forty to one for death over life. You can print infinite dollars.

53
00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:05.620
You cannot print geniuses. This is the most important sentence in this chapter.

54
00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:13.080
You will forget it by tomorrow because your brain allocated its attention budget the same way your government allocates

55
00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:18.640
its money. The Inflation Shell Game (How They Steal Medical Progress).

56
00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:26.240
Watch closely. This is how they rob you in broad daylight while you clap: Year 1.

57
